\ Second Genstat reference program for predictmeans (Genstat 21+). Please save the
\ whole Output window as a file (File > Save, .out or .txt) and send that file;
\ values typed by hand cannot be used as references. The first run may need
\ small syntax fixes.
\
\ Yates' oats split plot (nlme::Oats): Block 1-6 (I-VI), whole plots Variety
\ (1 GoldenRain, 2 Marvellous, 3 Victory), sub-plots Nitro (0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6).
\ Four patterns of missing data, each testing a different rule:
\   A. a whole plot (Block I x GoldenRain) and one sub-plot (Block II x Victory
\      x 0.6) missing, 67 observations: the data of SAS run 3 (dev/sas). The three
\      Kenward-Roger versions differ most here (Variety df 8.30 observed, 9.14
\      expected, 8.75 average information): which one Genstat's df are.
\   B. an empty cell: Victory x 0.6 missing in every block, 66 observations.
\      Nitro and Variety means over all cells cannot be estimated; predictmeans
\      averages the observed cells (as Genstat's PRESENT): do the means agree?
\   C. one sub-plot missing (Block II x Victory x 0.6), 71 observations:
\      ANOVA by strata (Genstat estimates the missing value) and REML. predictmeans
\      analyses aov(... Error()) by strata too, but combines the strata's
\      information instead of estimating the missing value: how far apart?
\   D. five scattered sub-plots missing, 67 observations: REML df when the
\      sub-plot stratum is unbalanced.

UNITS [NVALUES=72]
FACTOR [LEVELS=6] Block
FACTOR [LABELS=!t(GoldenRain, Marvellous, Victory)] Variety
FACTOR [LEVELS=!(0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6)] Nitro
VARIATE Yield
READ Block, Variety, Nitro, Yield
1 1 0.0 117   1 1 0.2 114   1 1 0.4 161   1 1 0.6 141
1 2 0.0 105   1 2 0.2 140   1 2 0.4 118   1 2 0.6 156
1 3 0.0 111   1 3 0.2 130   1 3 0.4 157   1 3 0.6 174
2 1 0.0 70   2 1 0.2 108   2 1 0.4 126   2 1 0.6 149
2 2 0.0 96   2 2 0.2 124   2 2 0.4 121   2 2 0.6 144
2 3 0.0 61   2 3 0.2 91   2 3 0.4 97   2 3 0.6 100
3 1 0.0 60   3 1 0.2 102   3 1 0.4 89   3 1 0.6 96
3 2 0.0 89   3 2 0.2 129   3 2 0.4 132   3 2 0.6 124
3 3 0.0 68   3 3 0.2 64   3 3 0.4 112   3 3 0.6 86
4 1 0.0 64   4 1 0.2 103   4 1 0.4 132   4 1 0.6 133
4 2 0.0 70   4 2 0.2 89   4 2 0.4 104   4 2 0.6 117
4 3 0.0 74   4 3 0.2 89   4 3 0.4 81   4 3 0.6 122
5 1 0.0 80   5 1 0.2 82   5 1 0.4 94   5 1 0.6 126
5 2 0.0 63   5 2 0.2 70   5 2 0.4 109   5 2 0.6 99
5 3 0.0 62   5 3 0.2 90   5 3 0.4 100   5 3 0.6 116
6 1 0.0 89   6 1 0.2 82   6 1 0.4 86   6 1 0.6 104
6 2 0.0 97   6 2 0.2 99   6 2 0.4 119   6 2 0.6 121
6 3 0.0 53   6 3 0.2 74   6 3 0.4 118   6 3 0.6 113
:
\ The four patterns: MVINSERT(x; test) sets x missing where test is true
\ (factors take their level values: Variety 1-3, Nitro 0-0.6).
CALCULATE YA = MVINSERT(Yield; ((Block.EQ.1).AND.(Variety.EQ.1)) .OR. \
                               ((Block.EQ.2).AND.(Variety.EQ.3).AND.(Nitro.EQ.0.6)))
CALCULATE YB = MVINSERT(Yield; (Variety.EQ.3).AND.(Nitro.EQ.0.6))
CALCULATE YC = MVINSERT(Yield; (Block.EQ.2).AND.(Variety.EQ.3).AND.(Nitro.EQ.0.6))
CALCULATE YD = MVINSERT(Yield; ((Block.EQ.1).AND.(Variety.EQ.2).AND.(Nitro.EQ.0.2)) .OR. \
                               ((Block.EQ.3).AND.(Variety.EQ.1).AND.(Nitro.EQ.0.6)) .OR. \
                               ((Block.EQ.4).AND.(Variety.EQ.3).AND.(Nitro.EQ.0))   .OR. \
                               ((Block.EQ.5).AND.(Variety.EQ.2).AND.(Nitro.EQ.0.4)) .OR. \
                               ((Block.EQ.6).AND.(Variety.EQ.1).AND.(Nitro.EQ.0.2)))
SCALAR nA, nB, nC, nD
CALCULATE nA, nB, nC, nD = NOBSERVATIONS(YA, YB, YC, YD)
PRINT nA, nB, nC, nD
\ (expected: 67, 66, 71, 67)

VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=Variety*Nitro] RANDOM=Block/Variety

\ ---- A. whole plot + one sub-plot missing (67) ----
REML [PRINT=model, components, waldtests, means; PTERMS=Variety + Nitro + Variety.Nitro; \
      PSE=differences; METHOD=AI] YA

\ ---- B. empty cell Victory x 0.6 (66) ----
REML [PRINT=model, components, waldtests, means; PTERMS=Variety + Nitro + Variety.Nitro; \
      PSE=differences; METHOD=AI] YB
\ means averaging only over the combinations present in the data (as predictmeans);
\ CLASSIFY is a parameter of VPREDICT; if PRESENTCOMBINATIONS=yes is not accepted,
\ the fault message lists the values it takes
VPREDICT [PRINT=description, predictions, se, sed; PRESENTCOMBINATIONS=yes] CLASSIFY=Nitro
VPREDICT [PRINT=description, predictions, se, sed; PRESENTCOMBINATIONS=yes] CLASSIFY=Variety

\ ---- C. one sub-plot missing (71): ANOVA by strata, then REML ----
BLOCKSTRUCTURE Block/Variety
TREATMENTSTRUCTURE Variety*Nitro
ANOVA [PRINT=aovtable, information, means, missingvalues; FPROBABILITY=yes; PSE=differences] YC
REML [PRINT=model, components, waldtests, means; PTERMS=Variety + Nitro + Variety.Nitro; \
      PSE=differences; METHOD=AI] YC

\ ---- D. five scattered sub-plots missing (67) ----
REML [PRINT=model, components, waldtests, means; PTERMS=Variety + Nitro + Variety.Nitro; \
      PSE=differences; METHOD=AI] YD
STOP
